WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:07.900
After the surgery . . . and you know the knee only rehabilitated back to a certain level,

2
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:15.900
so . . . I knew early that my chances of reaching that level were slim and slimmer.

3
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.860
The main thing I wanted to do was to finish.

4
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:22.000
A lot of guys that knew . . . that were injured and knew they weren’t . . . you know,

5
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.900
they just said, “Well, you know, why even do this anymore?

6
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.240
I have my scholarship.

7
00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.940
I’m just going to go to school and finish up and get on with my life.”

8
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:33.920
But, I wanted to finish.

9
00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.260
Finish as a player?

10
00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:37.320
As a player, yeah.

11
00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:42.620
So that’s kind of the way I pursued that.

12
00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:44.380
My last year, you know,

13
00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:52.700
the knee was just . . . it got to the point where I . . . a whole practice session was just too much,

14
00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:57.060
and then sprints afterwards, I just couldn’t do it.

15
00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:00.580
It was amazing because the coaches, they knew that.

16
00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:05.960
So they just said, “Well, look, why don’t you just kind of stay out of the sprints?”

17
00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:13.780
I tell you, it was a humbling situation, you know, because they . . . They knew what I was doing.

18
00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:17.240
You know, “He’s going to finish up with us.”

19
00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:22.080
They respected that so . . .

20
00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:23.347
And you finished up.

21
00:01:23.347 --> 00:01:23.680
That was nice.
